1
00:00:58,720 --> 00:00:59,760
Whoa!

2
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,360
Run!

3
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:19,880
It's the Zugor!

4
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,160
The Monster? Ah!

5
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:29,040
Ah!

6
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:36,240
Hey, hey, hey!
No fair catching a ride.

7
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,240
Oh! Ooh!

8
00:01:39,320 --> 00:01:40,840
Uh, hello.

9
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:43,320
What do you think you're doing?

10
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:46,080
'Cause whatever it is,
you sure ain't doing it
too good.

11
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,640
Is it still coming?

12
00:01:55,280 --> 00:01:57,520
Hey, wait a minute.

13
00:01:57,600 --> 00:02:00,320
There's no such thing
as the Zugor.

14
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:03,520
He's nothing but
an imaginary figment.

15
00:02:03,960 --> 00:02:07,040
Terk was just pretending
so I could practice running
for my life.

16
00:02:07,360 --> 00:02:09,240
I'm too slow.
If I don't get faster

17
00:02:09,320 --> 00:02:11,640
something terrible
is gonna get me.

18
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,560
You're the worst ape ever.

19
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:16,240
If the Zugor ever did come down
from Dark Mountain,

20
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,320
you'd be digested by now.

21
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:19,800
Well, I bet I could catch you.

22
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,760
- Could not.
- Roar!

23
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,240
- Missed me.
- Roar!

24
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,400
Missed again.

25
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:27,160
It's sad really.

26
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:31,680
This is a prescription
for disaster.

27
00:03:13,560 --> 00:03:15,920
Come on, you can make it.

28
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:24,440
You can make it.
You can make it.

29
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:40,360
Whoa!

30
00:03:44,280 --> 00:03:46,840
Watch out!

31
00:03:50,120 --> 00:03:52,760
Tree! Tree! Tree!

32
00:03:57,120 --> 00:04:02,000
STYLE
::cue

33
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,760
- You all right?
- Are you hurt?

34
00:04:08,840 --> 00:04:09,920
Let me see.

35
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,160
What is the matter with you?
He's only a baby.

36
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,240
I don't want you playing
with that one anymore.

37
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,200
Oh, he's going to
get somebody hurt.

38
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:20,920
He's a menace.

39
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:25,400
Nice. Almost wiped out
half the family.

40
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:27,960
Oh, it's Elephant Falls
all over again.

41
00:04:28,080 --> 00:04:30,640
Ooh, I can
just hear Kerchak.

42
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:34,080
"You almost killed someone."

43
00:04:34,160 --> 00:04:37,080
"He's only a child.
He'll learn."

44
00:04:37,160 --> 00:04:39,720
"He'll never survive
in the jungle.

45
00:04:39,840 --> 00:04:41,640
He can't run,
he can't climb.

46
00:04:41,760 --> 00:04:43,840
He's a danger to us all.

47
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:46,520
Now, I think I'll grunt
impressively."

48
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:57,840
Hey, pal.
You know I'm kidding, right?

49
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:00,600
Sure.

50
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:06,440
I wasn't making fun of you.
I was making fun of Kerchak.

51
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:08,560
Eww.

52
00:05:50,720 --> 00:05:54,400
Come on, time for bed.

53
00:05:54,480 --> 00:05:57,080
Let's see now...

54
00:05:57,920 --> 00:06:01,160
There. How's that?
Comfy?

55
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,520
It's great, Mom.

56
00:06:05,280 --> 00:06:08,000
I've got your nose.

57
00:06:08,080 --> 00:06:12,520
- I've got your toes.
- Mom, stop.

58
00:06:12,640 --> 00:06:14,760
I'm too big
for "nose and toes."

59
00:06:14,840 --> 00:06:17,840
Uh-oh. I think one is missing.

60
00:06:17,920 --> 00:06:20,560
Maybe you're hiding it in...

61
00:06:20,640 --> 00:06:23,760
- ...here.
- Mom, stop.

62
00:06:23,840 --> 00:06:26,440
Stop. No, really...

63
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:30,080
Mom, stop it.

64
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:33,960
Tarzan, what's wrong?

65
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:39,360
- Tarzan?
- I'm not a good ape.

66
00:06:39,440 --> 00:06:42,040
I can't outrun the Zugor.

67
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:45,320
The Zugor?
You know there's no such thing.

68
00:06:45,400 --> 00:06:47,360
That's just an old ghost story.

69
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:50,040
But if he was real,
he'd get me.

70
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:52,360
I'm too slow.

71
00:06:52,440 --> 00:06:55,680
I'll tell you what,
if the Zugor ever comes for you,

72
00:06:55,760 --> 00:06:58,720
I'll save you.
You can count on it.

73
00:06:58,800 --> 00:07:03,040
But, then you'd be in danger
because of me.

74
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:07,200
Everyone would be better off
if I just wasn't around.

75
00:07:07,280 --> 00:07:12,680
Come with me.
I want to show you something.

76
00:07:23,840 --> 00:07:27,720
This tree used to stand here,
all by itself.

77
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:31,080
What happened to it?

78
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,560
Oh, one day
there was a big storm,

79
00:07:32,640 --> 00:07:37,000
and the wind pulled on the tree,
until finally it blew over.

80
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:40,120
But now, look over here.

81
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:55,440
This is the strongest tree
in the jungle,

82
00:07:55,520 --> 00:07:58,080
because it has many trunks,
all working together,

83
00:07:58,200 --> 00:08:00,880
lifting the leaves into the sky.

84
00:08:00,960 --> 00:08:03,560
And look, the trunks
are all different.

85
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:05,720
Some are thin, some thick,

86
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:07,720
some twisted, some straight.
STYLE
::cue

87
00:08:07,840 --> 00:08:10,640
That one looks fat.

88
00:08:10,720 --> 00:08:12,600
It does, doesn't it?

89
00:08:12,720 --> 00:08:16,400
But, they all help
make the tree strong,

90
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:19,440
strong enough
to weather any storm.

91
00:08:19,520 --> 00:08:21,200
Like a family.

92
00:08:22,600 --> 00:08:25,240
- Like our family?
- That's right.

93
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:28,800
You need your family, Tarzan,
and your family needs you.

94
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:32,120
- Nobody needs me.
- I do.

95
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:37,600
And I always will.

96
00:08:37,680 --> 00:08:40,080
Now, where is that missing toe?

97
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:42,600
Mom,
I've got all my toes.

98
00:08:42,680 --> 00:08:45,920
No, don't think so.
Maybe it's here. Or here...

99
00:08:46,040 --> 00:08:47,920
Mom, stop.

100
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,640
- Whoa!
- Roar!

101
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,000
Ooh, teeth.

102
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:13,480
Look out for the big
scary teeth.

103
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:17,880
Run! Run!
It's the Zugor! Whoa!

104
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:13,520
Quit playing around, Tarzan.

105
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:17,320
So, what are we waiting for?

106
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:30,120
Run!

107
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:52,080
Ah!

108
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,360
- Tarzan!
- Mom!

109
00:11:40,080 --> 00:11:42,160
No.

110
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:53,080
Kala.
STYLE
::cue

111
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:13,640
Mom?

112
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,760
Mom?

113
00:12:16,880 --> 00:12:20,960
Where is everybody?

114
00:12:21,040 --> 00:12:24,000
Mom, where are you?

115
00:12:24,080 --> 00:12:25,520
I'm sorry, Kala.

116
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:29,720
He was there.
I almost had him.

117
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:33,560
And then he was... No.

118
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:35,800
There is nothing you
could have done.

119
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:39,480
I would have done anything.
I would have given my life
for his.

120
00:12:43,120 --> 00:12:46,240
It was horrible.

121
00:12:46,320 --> 00:12:48,080
He almost got her killed too.

122
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:50,880
I hate to say it,

123
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:54,080
but she's probably
better off without him.

124
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:55,800
I think we all are.

125
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,800
Ah!

126
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,400
Ah!

127
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:43,640
Zugor!
STYLE
::cue

128
00:16:23,480 --> 00:16:27,520
Eh?

129
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:46,480
- Huh?
- Look what I got.
It's a little bird.

130
00:16:46,560 --> 00:16:49,640
- But I'm not a bird.
- Kago, look what I got.

131
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:51,480
- A little bird.
- Huh?

132
00:16:51,560 --> 00:16:53,120
Huh?

133
00:16:57,120 --> 00:17:01,040
Can't you see I was
enjoying myself? I ought to...

134
00:17:01,520 --> 00:17:03,480
- Wait a second.
- Hey!

135
00:17:03,560 --> 00:17:07,320
- Uto, that's not a bird.
- So not.

136
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:10,680
It hasn't got any feathers,
banana brain.

137
00:17:10,800 --> 00:17:13,480
Is too, and I can prove it.

138
00:17:13,560 --> 00:17:16,840
We'll throw it off a cliff
and when it flies,

139
00:17:16,920 --> 00:17:21,200
then you'll be the banana brain.

140
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:24,960
Don't poke me.

141
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:28,840
Don't poke me!
Don't poke me! Don't poke me!

142
00:17:31,040 --> 00:17:32,840
Stop! Stop!

143
00:17:32,920 --> 00:17:34,920
Stop laughing!

144
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,080
I like it when my brother
gets hiccups.

145
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:38,920
It's hilarious.

146
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,040
That's it.

147
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:43,800
I'm taking you down.

148
00:17:49,640 --> 00:17:52,280
Boys!

149
00:17:52,360 --> 00:17:53,960
- Hi, Ma.
- Hello, Mother.

150
00:17:55,360 --> 00:17:59,040
My darling boys,
my little treasures,

151
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,880
what has Mama Gunda
told you about fighting?

152
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:04,440
- But he was poking me.
- He called me banana brain.

153
00:18:06,360 --> 00:18:08,080
Lips!

154
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:12,600
Fighting each other
makes Mama...

155
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:15,760
...very unhappy!

156
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:18,400
Do we understand Mama?

157
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:21,200
Yes, ma'am.

158
00:18:21,280 --> 00:18:25,720
What is all this silliness
about a baby bird, hmm?

159
00:18:25,800 --> 00:18:28,640
I'm not a bird.
I'm an ape.

160
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:33,840
- An ape!
- Like you.

161
00:18:37,120 --> 00:18:39,280
Can we still throw it
off a cliff?

162
00:18:39,360 --> 00:18:42,280
If you are an ape,
where's your family?

163
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:44,840
- How did you get here?
- Uh...

164
00:18:44,920 --> 00:18:47,040
You must have come through
that rift.

165
00:18:47,120 --> 00:18:49,120
It's the only way in.

166
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:50,720
Besides falling in.

167
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:54,040
I tripped.
I was trying to get
away from the monster.

168
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:55,640
We all were, dear.

169
00:18:55,720 --> 00:18:56,640
Monster?

170
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:59,680
It guards the rift,
just waiting.

171
00:18:59,760 --> 00:19:04,400
And if it catches you,
they say it'll eat you.

172
00:19:04,480 --> 00:19:06,080
They call it...

173
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:08,000
- Don't say it, Ma.
- I'm not listening.

174
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:10,440
La, la, la, la, la.
I don't hear this.

175
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:12,600
...the Zugor.

176
00:19:12,680 --> 00:19:14,680
But there's no such thing
as the Zu...

177
00:19:14,800 --> 00:19:20,600
Zugor!

178
00:19:20,720 --> 00:19:22,520
It's coming.

179
00:19:22,640 --> 00:19:27,800
Ah! The Zugor!

180
00:19:32,040 --> 00:19:34,920
Zugor!

181
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,080
Whoa!

182
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:38,800
Ay!

183
00:19:39,360 --> 00:19:41,320
Whoa!

184
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:51,920
Ah!

185
00:19:57,560 --> 00:20:00,480
It's the Zugor!
Run, it's the Zugor!

186
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:03,360
- Ah!
- Ah!

187
00:20:07,680 --> 00:20:08,800
Oof!

188
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:11,640
My tree. Stay out.
STYLE
::cue

189
00:20:11,720 --> 00:20:15,080
- But you've gotta let me...
- No. Go away.

190
00:20:17,360 --> 00:20:19,440
- Please!
- No.

191
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:22,080
If I stay out here
the Zugor might get me.

192
00:20:22,160 --> 00:20:25,320
Boo-hoo for you.

193
00:20:25,400 --> 00:20:28,640
You've got to help me.

194
00:20:28,720 --> 00:20:31,680
You've got to.

195
00:20:55,760 --> 00:20:58,520
Mom?

196
00:21:15,240 --> 00:21:19,560
Okay, my babies.
There we go, climb in.

197
00:21:25,240 --> 00:21:30,400
Oh, it's been another big day
for my two little boys,
hasn't it?

198
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:32,760
The Zugor scared us, Ma.

199
00:21:32,840 --> 00:21:34,920
Oh, I know, dear.

200
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
- Didn't scare me.
- Did too.

201
00:21:37,080 --> 00:21:40,680
- Did not.
- Did too.

202
00:21:40,760 --> 00:21:43,800
Did not.

203
00:21:51,400 --> 00:21:53,440
- Ma?
- Yes, dear?

204
00:21:53,520 --> 00:21:56,760
- Tell us a story.
- All right.

205
00:21:56,840 --> 00:22:00,200
If I tell you a story,
will you go to sleep for Mama?

206
00:22:00,280 --> 00:22:01,440
Yes, ma'am.

207
00:22:01,520 --> 00:22:04,040
Well, then, let's see.

208
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:08,760
All right. Once upon a time,
there was a family of three...

209
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:11,440
...oh, oh, I don't know,
three...

210
00:22:11,520 --> 00:22:14,240
- Silly little froggies?
- All right, dear.

211
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:19,360
Once upon a time there was
a family of three little frogs.

212
00:22:19,480 --> 00:22:22,720
One of them
was a tiny bit dim...

213
00:22:22,800 --> 00:22:26,680
- Which one?
- One was a teensy bit violent.

214
00:22:26,760 --> 00:22:28,160
I like that one.

215
00:22:28,280 --> 00:22:33,040
And some might say the mama
was just a tad controlling...

216
00:22:33,120 --> 00:22:35,200
...but, I disagree.

217
00:22:35,280 --> 00:22:38,720
Do alligators eat the frogs?

218
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:41,560
Oh, no. Don't let
the froggies get eaten.

219
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:43,080
Have them fly away.

220
00:22:43,160 --> 00:22:46,240
It's all right, Uto,
they don't get eaten.

221
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:50,160
But the three
little frogs were all alone

222
00:22:50,240 --> 00:22:53,120
in a great big world,

223
00:22:53,200 --> 00:22:55,520
hopping from pond to pond.

224
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,200
Hippety-hop.

225
00:22:57,280 --> 00:23:01,760
Just trying to find somewhere
where they'd be wanted.

226
00:23:01,840 --> 00:23:06,480
But every place they went,
they were kicked out.

227
00:23:06,560 --> 00:23:09,760
Maybe the frogs need to
smash some heads, Ma!

228
00:23:09,840 --> 00:23:13,440
- Yeah.
- The frogs ended up
in a horrible valley,

229
00:23:13,520 --> 00:23:15,360
terrorized by a monster,

230
00:23:15,440 --> 00:23:18,440
with next to nothing
to eat or drink

231
00:23:18,520 --> 00:23:23,280
and only pointy rocks
to sleep on!

232
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:25,960
- So...
- Huh?

233
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:31,760
...tomorrow she's gonna
find her froggies a new home.

234
00:23:31,840 --> 00:23:36,800
And this time anyone who
gets in her way is gonna feel

235
00:23:36,880 --> 00:23:42,320
the terrible wrath
of Mama Frog!

236
00:23:44,120 --> 00:23:47,440
Mom, I broke my pillow...

237
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,880
...again.

238
00:24:02,240 --> 00:24:03,960
Tarzan?

239
00:24:04,040 --> 00:24:06,920
Mom!
STYLE
::cue

240
00:24:51,880 --> 00:24:53,680
Ouch.

241
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:09,760
Zugor!

242
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:22,840
Zugor!

243
00:26:24,800 --> 00:26:27,640
Zugor!

244
00:26:29,840 --> 00:26:32,320
The Zugor?

245
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:34,160
I don't believe it.

246
00:26:44,120 --> 00:26:46,480
- Hi, Zugor.
- Hello.

247
00:26:47,800 --> 00:26:50,760
You are the Zugor,
aren't you?

248
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:53,880
- No, I'm not.
- Sure you are. I saw you.

249
00:26:53,960 --> 00:26:56,400
- No, you didn't.
- You scared off that rhino

250
00:26:56,480 --> 00:26:58,040
so you could get this fruit.

251
00:26:58,120 --> 00:27:01,000
Hey, that's mine!

252
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:10,600
- Run!
- Ah!

253
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:13,200
Whoa!

254
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:41,280
Huh?

255
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,200
Gee, thanks...

256
00:27:48,240 --> 00:27:49,800
...for nothing!

257
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:52,560
Your fault we were being
chased in the first place.

258
00:27:52,640 --> 00:27:55,080
- Hey, wait up.
STYLE
::cue
- Hey, wait up.

259
00:27:57,440 --> 00:27:58,760
Go away.

260
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:03,200
Leave me alone.

261
00:28:03,280 --> 00:28:06,760
- Alone?
- Yes, alone.

262
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:10,680
Don't need anyone but yourself.

263
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,960
Go home.

264
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:16,280
- I can't. I ran away.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

265
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:17,680
And I can't go back,

266
00:28:17,760 --> 00:28:19,760
not until I learn
how to be a good ape.

267
00:28:19,880 --> 00:28:22,440
Boo-hoo.
Go play with an alligator.

268
00:28:22,520 --> 00:28:26,640
Hey, maybe you could teach me?
You're the Zugor.

269
00:28:26,720 --> 00:28:28,800
Teach? Me? Nah.

270
00:28:28,880 --> 00:28:31,720
Wait... Nah.

271
00:28:31,800 --> 00:28:34,280
Nah!

272
00:28:34,400 --> 00:28:36,040
So long, goodbye, toodle-oo.

273
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:49,520
Okay, I guess I'll be going.

274
00:28:49,600 --> 00:28:53,760
Boy, I can't wait
to tell everyone who
the Zugor really is.

275
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:54,760
Huh?

276
00:28:54,880 --> 00:28:58,040
Especially those three big apes.

277
00:28:58,120 --> 00:29:00,120
Gosh, I bet we have a good laugh

278
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:02,440
when I tell them
you're the Zugor.

279
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:04,200
Whoa, whoa, whoa.

280
00:29:04,280 --> 00:29:07,880
Hmm. You know you could
change your mind.

281
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:10,240
That way, I'll never
tell anyone your secret.

282
00:29:12,280 --> 00:29:13,920
I don't like you.

283
00:29:18,960 --> 00:29:22,440
Oh, fine. Deal.
I'll help you.

284
00:29:22,520 --> 00:29:25,120
And in return
you don't tell anyone.

285
00:29:25,240 --> 00:29:31,200
Right!
Don't tell anyone.

286
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:37,840
Tarzan?

287
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,720
You can't catch me,
Zugor.

288
00:29:58,800 --> 00:30:01,080
Not now, guys, okay?

289
00:30:01,160 --> 00:30:03,920
I'm not in the mood.

290
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:10,600
Hey! I said I'm not in the mood,
okay? Now get lost!

291
00:30:16,440 --> 00:30:18,040
Oh...

292
00:30:18,120 --> 00:30:20,960
Look. I'm sorry, okay?

293
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:26,960
The game wouldn't be the same
without Tarzan, you know?

294
00:30:27,800 --> 00:30:30,080
I can't believe he's gone.

295
00:30:32,040 --> 00:30:35,360
Terk! Tarzan's alive!

296
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:37,560
- That's impossible.
- But, I heard him.

297
00:30:37,640 --> 00:30:40,280
He was saying,
"Don't tell anyone."

298
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:42,080
You've been soaking
in the sun too long.

299
00:30:42,160 --> 00:30:44,040
Take two mangoes
and call me in the morning.

300
00:30:44,120 --> 00:30:48,040
I heard Tarzan's voice coming
from up on Dark Mountain.

301
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:49,800
Why didn't anyone else hear it?
STYLE
::cue

302
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:54,360
I'm an elephant.
I've got 20/20 hearing.

303
00:30:56,080 --> 00:31:01,080
Okay. Let's see
if we can find him.

304
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:08,240
Terk, Tarzan said
not to tell anyone.

305
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:10,880
Huh? Oh.

306
00:31:10,960 --> 00:31:12,320
Whoa, whoa.

307
00:31:12,400 --> 00:31:14,360
Uh, you guys
have to stay here.

308
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,560
- Nuh-uh.
- No, we don't.

309
00:31:16,640 --> 00:31:19,000
Yeah, you do.
You, um...

310
00:31:19,080 --> 00:31:23,560
You need to stay behind
and, uh... cover for us. Yeah.

311
00:31:23,640 --> 00:31:25,520
If anybody asks,

312
00:31:25,600 --> 00:31:29,680
tell them we're out
picking monkey berries.

313
00:31:29,760 --> 00:31:30,920
- Got it?
- Oh. Okay.

314
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:32,680
Monkey berries.
Got it.

315
00:31:32,760 --> 00:31:36,240
Yeah, you're very cute, okay.
Run along, run along.

316
00:31:43,320 --> 00:31:45,560
Terk was trying
to teach me to be a good ape

317
00:31:45,640 --> 00:31:47,160
so she pretended to be
a monster.

318
00:31:47,240 --> 00:31:48,880
I mean, she was pretending
to be you,

319
00:31:48,960 --> 00:31:51,880
but you're not a monster.
You're a Zugor who pretends...

320
00:31:54,200 --> 00:31:57,680
Hey! Wait for me!

321
00:31:57,760 --> 00:31:59,720
Wow. This is your home?
Where do you sleep?

322
00:31:59,800 --> 00:32:01,840
This place is great.
You have your own stream.

323
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:04,280
Bah, bah, bah.

324
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:07,040
Now, in as few words
as possible,

325
00:32:07,120 --> 00:32:09,200
what do I gotta do
to get rid of you?

326
00:32:09,320 --> 00:32:11,040
Teach me how
to be a good ape.

327
00:32:11,120 --> 00:32:15,120
An ape?
Kid, you're not an ape.

328
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,480
I am too.

329
00:32:18,560 --> 00:32:22,080
Nope. I'll prove it to you.

330
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:24,560
hair.

331
00:32:24,640 --> 00:32:28,240
no hair.

332
00:32:28,320 --> 00:32:30,840
Not an ape.

333
00:32:32,040 --> 00:32:34,240
But... but I gotta be.

334
00:32:34,320 --> 00:32:37,240
My mom's an ape,
my friends are apes,

335
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:38,920
my whole family.

336
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:41,520
If I'm not an ape then...

337
00:32:41,600 --> 00:32:43,080
Then...

338
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:45,600
...what am I?

339
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:46,880
Hmm...

340
00:32:46,960 --> 00:32:48,760
I don't know.

341
00:32:48,840 --> 00:32:51,440
Maybe you're some form
of mutant hairless gibbon.

342
00:32:51,520 --> 00:32:54,800
- A gibbon?
- Or a variety of annoying
featherless bird.

343
00:32:54,880 --> 00:32:56,000
A bird?

344
00:32:56,080 --> 00:32:59,760
Or perhaps some rare species
of ugly fish.

345
00:32:59,840 --> 00:33:02,080
- Ugly?
- Oh, yes.

346
00:33:02,160 --> 00:33:05,520
Very, very, very ugly.

347
00:33:07,120 --> 00:33:09,880
There, figured out
you're not an ape.
That about wraps it up.

348
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:12,440
Can't teach you to be something
you're not. Bye.

349
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:13,560
Whoa, wait.

350
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,560
You still gotta help me
find out what I am.

351
00:33:15,680 --> 00:33:19,040
We have a deal... Zugor.

352
00:33:23,720 --> 00:33:25,040
Fine.

353
00:33:25,120 --> 00:33:26,800
Ah, Zugor, thank you so...

354
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:27,800
Hold it.

355
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:30,360
No sappy "thank you's"

356
00:33:30,440 --> 00:33:33,800
will be encouraged, indulged
or even barely tolerated.

357
00:33:33,880 --> 00:33:36,160
Now, come on. The sooner
we figure out what you are,

358
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:38,160
the sooner I can be rid of you.

359
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:39,240
Okay.

360
00:33:39,320 --> 00:33:41,320
- Hey, Zugor.
- Huh?

361
00:33:41,400 --> 00:33:44,680
- Thanks anyway.
- Bah.
STYLE
::cue
- Thanks anyway.
- Bah.

362
00:35:32,640 --> 00:35:35,000
You know what, kid?
You got pluck.

363
00:35:36,120 --> 00:35:38,320
I hate pluck.

364
00:35:50,800 --> 00:35:55,760
I am the Zugor. Roar!

365
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:19,640
- Auntie Kala's sad.
- How come?

366
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:21,920
She misses Tarzan.

367
00:36:22,000 --> 00:36:23,800
That's right, little one.

368
00:36:23,880 --> 00:36:25,680
Oh, don't cry,
Tarzan's still...

369
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,760
- Monkey berries.
- Remember?

370
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:31,160
I know.
I wasn't gonna tell her.

371
00:36:31,240 --> 00:36:33,440
- Tell me what?
- That Tarzan's alive.

372
00:36:33,520 --> 00:36:35,120
Terk and Tantor
went to look for him.

373
00:36:35,200 --> 00:36:36,120
Oh!

374
00:36:36,200 --> 00:36:37,680
On Dark Mountain.

375
00:36:40,360 --> 00:36:41,960
Tarzan's alive?

376
00:36:43,440 --> 00:36:46,720
I'm going to look for them.
You kids stay here.

377
00:37:01,400 --> 00:37:03,920
Well, today
didn't work out too good.

378
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:07,240
Oh! But we'll try again
tomorrow, right?

379
00:37:07,320 --> 00:37:10,000
Oh, I'm eager, excited,

380
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:12,440
breathless with anticipation.

381
00:37:12,520 --> 00:37:14,160
Enough yapping out of you.

382
00:37:14,240 --> 00:37:17,720
Less yapping,
more napping.

383
00:37:19,920 --> 00:37:21,920
Uh-uh-uh.

384
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:23,440
Me, here.

385
00:37:23,520 --> 00:37:26,400
You, there.

386
00:37:26,480 --> 00:37:28,840
Way over there.

387
00:37:32,160 --> 00:37:34,360
Me Tarzan, you grouch.

388
00:37:34,480 --> 00:37:36,600
STYLE
::cue

389
00:37:51,160 --> 00:37:52,480
Old bones.

390
00:37:52,560 --> 00:37:54,280
You need a better nest.

391
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:57,520
My mom could make
a really good nest.

392
00:37:57,600 --> 00:38:01,160
Yeah. My mom made
a great nest too.

393
00:38:01,440 --> 00:38:02,400
Nice.

394
00:38:02,480 --> 00:38:04,320
- Soft.
- Warm.

395
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:08,640
She made me this nest once,
swung between two branches.

396
00:38:08,720 --> 00:38:12,880
Like sleeping on air.

397
00:38:15,440 --> 00:38:18,200
So when did you figure out
you were a Zugor?

398
00:38:18,280 --> 00:38:20,720
That's past.

399
00:38:20,800 --> 00:38:23,200
- All in the past.
- What happened?

400
00:38:23,280 --> 00:38:25,040
Got old. Got slow.
Got left behind.

401
00:38:25,120 --> 00:38:27,920
Same old story.
Boo-hoo. How sad for me.

402
00:38:29,280 --> 00:38:30,960
A danger to the family.

403
00:38:33,280 --> 00:38:34,800
I'm gonna go take a look around.

404
00:38:34,880 --> 00:38:37,040
Got to keep an eye out.
Keep them away.

405
00:38:37,120 --> 00:38:39,080
- Rule Number One.
- Can I help?

406
00:38:40,600 --> 00:38:42,800
No.

407
00:38:52,400 --> 00:38:54,440
Uh, Terk,

408
00:38:54,560 --> 00:38:58,400
isn't Dark Mountain
where the Zugor lives?

409
00:38:58,480 --> 00:39:01,440
Don't worry about that.

410
00:39:01,520 --> 00:39:05,280
Zugor is just an imaginary
figment, remember?

411
00:39:05,360 --> 00:39:07,760
He's not real.

412
00:39:07,840 --> 00:39:11,000
Sure, you know that
and I know that,

413
00:39:11,120 --> 00:39:13,160
but does he know that?

414
00:39:13,240 --> 00:39:17,680
Zugor!

415
00:39:18,880 --> 00:39:22,440
- Go on. Shoo!
- Ah!

416
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:25,680
I do believe in Zugors!
I do believe in Zugors!
I do! I do! I do!

417
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:36,280
Huh?

418
00:39:36,360 --> 00:39:37,680
Gotcha.

419
00:39:37,760 --> 00:39:41,760
- You got him all right, Kago.
- Hey, let me up.

420
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:46,360
Uh, Kago?
This isn't a baby bird.

421
00:39:46,440 --> 00:39:49,400
- It isn't?
- Uh, no, it isn't.

422
00:39:52,080 --> 00:39:54,960
Hey, you can't do that
to my brother.

423
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:58,360
Ah!

424
00:40:02,080 --> 00:40:04,520
Oh, no.
The Zugor has Terk.

425
00:40:06,480 --> 00:40:08,920
Leave my friend alone!

426
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:12,160
Take me instead!

427
00:40:12,240 --> 00:40:15,200
- Whoa!
- You want a piece of me?

428
00:40:15,280 --> 00:40:18,880
She's being eaten.
Oh, the horror!

429
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:23,160
Now, what are we
going to do with you?

430
00:40:23,240 --> 00:40:24,600
Oh, oh! I know.

431
00:40:24,680 --> 00:40:28,000
Let's throw her off a cliff
and see if she can fly.

432
00:40:28,080 --> 00:40:30,360
Gorillas can't fly.

433
00:40:30,440 --> 00:40:32,760
Oh yeah, how do you know?

434
00:40:32,840 --> 00:40:35,400
Because we are gorillas.

435
00:40:35,480 --> 00:40:39,240
- So?
- And we can't fly.

436
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:41,920
Yeah, but if our bones
were hollow,

437
00:40:42,040 --> 00:40:44,240
and we had wings
and feathers,

438
00:40:44,320 --> 00:40:46,800
we'd be the biggest birds
in town.

439
00:40:46,880 --> 00:40:49,680
Well,
what in the world...?

440
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:51,920
Look Ma, we found a gorilla.

441
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,520
And just where

442
00:40:53,600 --> 00:40:57,240
did this cute little sweetums
come from?

443
00:40:57,320 --> 00:40:59,440
Hey, hey.
Enough already, lady.

444
00:40:59,520 --> 00:41:01,360
I need that cheek for eating.

445
00:41:01,440 --> 00:41:06,400
Oh, aren't you
just the precocious one.

446
00:41:06,480 --> 00:41:08,720
Where are you from, dear?

447
00:41:08,800 --> 00:41:13,440
Tell us about your family, huh?
Is there a silverback?

448
00:41:13,520 --> 00:41:14,480
Forget it, lady.

449
00:41:14,560 --> 00:41:18,000
I'm not talking
and you can't make me.

450
00:41:18,080 --> 00:41:20,840
Kago.

451
00:41:31,440 --> 00:41:35,880
Let's try that again,
shall we, dear?

452
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:39,680
Now, how did you
get past the Zugor?

453
00:41:39,760 --> 00:41:44,000
And where exactly did you
say your family is from?
STYLE
::cue

454
00:41:44,080 --> 00:41:48,640
Is it nice?
Lots of food and water?

455
00:41:48,720 --> 00:41:52,480
Perhaps you could show us
the way sometime.

456
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:55,440
Terk?
Are you out there

457
00:41:55,520 --> 00:41:59,200
or are you all eaten?

458
00:41:59,280 --> 00:42:01,600
I don't want anybody
marching around my mountain,

459
00:42:01,680 --> 00:42:04,840
soiling my soil,
messing with my stuff.

460
00:42:04,960 --> 00:42:06,600
It's my stuff.

461
00:42:06,680 --> 00:42:10,720
Hey! Why are you messing
with my stuff?

462
00:42:10,800 --> 00:42:12,720
I made you a nest.

463
00:42:12,840 --> 00:42:15,200
You made this?

464
00:42:15,280 --> 00:42:18,200
- For me?
- Sure. For your old bones.

465
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:21,360
Like your mom used to make.
Try it out.

466
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:33,120
This wasn't part of the deal.

467
00:42:33,200 --> 00:42:34,800
I know.

468
00:42:39,240 --> 00:42:44,440
Ah... It's good.

469
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:48,000
Sleeping on air.

470
00:42:48,080 --> 00:42:51,160
I don't know
what you are, Tarzan,

471
00:42:51,240 --> 00:42:52,920
but you're pretty clever.

472
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:56,160
Like the other day when you
did that nifty vine thing
with the rhino.

473
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:58,480
Boing!

474
00:42:58,560 --> 00:43:02,480
- Never seen anything like it.
- Huh, yeah well,

475
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:05,400
I'm not smart enough
to figure out what I am though.

476
00:43:05,520 --> 00:43:09,160
I'm not strong like an elephant.
Not tall like a giraffe.

477
00:43:09,240 --> 00:43:11,720
I can't fly like a bird.

478
00:43:15,320 --> 00:43:17,400
Maybe I'm a nothing.

479
00:43:58,560 --> 00:44:02,560
So, you're just gonna sit here
and hold onto me

480
00:44:02,640 --> 00:44:04,520
until your mama comes back?

481
00:44:04,600 --> 00:44:06,000
Yep.

482
00:44:06,120 --> 00:44:08,720
- All day long?
- Yep.

483
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:12,080
I'm gonna smash you.

484
00:44:19,400 --> 00:44:21,880
Say, Uto,

485
00:44:21,960 --> 00:44:25,480
how come you gotta do all
the hard work around here? Huh?

486
00:44:25,600 --> 00:44:27,840
Huh? What? Hard work?

487
00:44:27,920 --> 00:44:31,440
I mean, you gotta sit here
with me while lazy Kago there

488
00:44:31,520 --> 00:44:33,560
gets to have fun
beating up his rock.

489
00:44:33,640 --> 00:44:37,760
I mean, I don't know,
but that just don't seem fair.

490
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:43,440
Nope, not fair at all.
Not even a little bit fair.

491
00:44:43,520 --> 00:44:45,360
Huh?

492
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:51,200
Hmm...

493
00:44:51,280 --> 00:44:53,920
Hmm... Eh?

494
00:44:54,000 --> 00:44:56,520
Say, this isn't fair.

495
00:44:56,600 --> 00:44:59,360
- What?
- I said this isn't fair.

496
00:44:59,440 --> 00:45:01,600
Me doing all the hard work.

497
00:45:01,680 --> 00:45:05,680
You gotta do some work too,
so here, Mr. Lazy.

498
00:45:05,760 --> 00:45:07,800
Are you gonna take that?

499
00:45:07,880 --> 00:45:10,800
- Take what?
- Uto insulted you.

500
00:45:10,880 --> 00:45:12,120
- He insulted me?
- Yes.

501
00:45:12,200 --> 00:45:15,360
- You insulted me?
- Uh... yes?

502
00:45:15,440 --> 00:45:17,800
Ooh! I'll...

503
00:45:19,680 --> 00:45:25,520
No idea
who you're dealing with.

504
00:45:27,240 --> 00:45:28,920
Stop.

505
00:45:29,040 --> 00:45:30,320
- Uto, stop.
- Huh?

506
00:45:30,400 --> 00:45:32,720
- Where is she?
- Oops.

507
00:45:32,800 --> 00:45:35,320
Just wait till I
catch her again.

508
00:45:35,400 --> 00:45:39,240
I'll... I'll...

509
00:45:39,320 --> 00:45:42,120
STYLE
::cue

510
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:24,880
Hey, you got a banana.
Good job.

511
00:46:24,960 --> 00:46:27,760
Not really.
If I was a chimp or a baboon,

512
00:46:27,840 --> 00:46:30,440
I'd just climb to the top
and get a whole bunch.

513
00:46:30,560 --> 00:46:33,040
I can only get one at a time.

514
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:37,120
Still think you're a nothing,
huh?

515
00:46:38,320 --> 00:46:41,600
Hmm. Maybe we can do
something about that.

516
00:46:41,680 --> 00:46:44,560
- We can?
- Yeah, I figure,

517
00:46:44,640 --> 00:46:46,760
since you're nothing,

518
00:46:46,840 --> 00:46:49,520
and you're looking
to be something...

519
00:46:49,600 --> 00:46:54,320
...you might as well
try being a Zugor.

520
00:46:54,400 --> 00:46:57,640
Hmm. A Zugor?

521
00:46:57,720 --> 00:47:00,200
It's fine if you don't want to.
Feel free to say no.

522
00:47:03,040 --> 00:47:06,920
After all,
it can get pretty lonely.

523
00:47:07,000 --> 00:47:10,520
You mean, I'd be like you?

524
00:47:16,160 --> 00:47:18,640
Wow! A Zugor!

525
00:47:18,720 --> 00:47:21,600
Yes! I'm a Zugor.

526
00:47:21,680 --> 00:47:24,560
Roar!

527
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:30,800
We don't need anyone
but ourselves.

528
00:47:30,880 --> 00:47:35,200
This is our mountain.
Roar!

529
00:47:35,280 --> 00:47:37,600
Our mountain.

530
00:47:39,200 --> 00:47:40,800
Zugor in training,

531
00:47:40,880 --> 00:47:43,720
use that vine thing of yours
to round up some breakfast.

532
00:47:43,840 --> 00:47:46,640
Yes, sir.

533
00:47:46,720 --> 00:47:49,400
- Zugor?
- Hmm?

534
00:47:54,200 --> 00:47:57,840
You know,
this wasn't part of the deal.

535
00:47:57,920 --> 00:47:59,600
I know.

536
00:48:06,160 --> 00:48:10,280
Hello? Is anyone there?

537
00:48:10,360 --> 00:48:13,840
Hello?

538
00:48:16,480 --> 00:48:20,120
Ah! Something's got me.
It's the monster!

539
00:48:20,200 --> 00:48:22,760
Goodbye cruel jungle world.

540
00:48:22,880 --> 00:48:25,600
I'm doomed. Doomed.

541
00:48:25,680 --> 00:48:28,200
Doomed to be a coconut head.

542
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:30,880
- Terk?
- The one and only.

543
00:48:30,960 --> 00:48:33,200
- Let's get out of here.
- Whoa!

544
00:48:41,800 --> 00:48:43,640
Terk? Tantor?

545
00:48:43,720 --> 00:48:48,360
Tarzan! You're alive!
You're alive!

546
00:48:48,440 --> 00:48:50,400
We thought you were dead
and then Tantor...

547
00:48:50,480 --> 00:48:53,960
Heard you yell, but when we
got to Dark Mountain,
the Zugor...

548
00:48:54,040 --> 00:48:56,080
And then those big apes...

549
00:48:57,480 --> 00:49:00,320
And then I was stuck in a hole
and Terk got eaten.

550
00:49:00,400 --> 00:49:02,240
Uh... sort of.

551
00:49:02,320 --> 00:49:04,640
Wait a minute,
those big apes are after you?

552
00:49:04,720 --> 00:49:06,400
They're probably
right behind us.

553
00:49:06,480 --> 00:49:09,640
Come on.
I know a great place to hide.

554
00:49:09,760 --> 00:49:13,720
Oh, what a sweet reunion.

555
00:49:13,800 --> 00:49:18,160
We're sorry we let her get away.
But she's an evil genius.

556
00:49:18,240 --> 00:49:21,760
It's all right, boys.
Now we can follow them.

557
00:49:21,840 --> 00:49:25,360
- Where, Ma?
- Past the Zugor, of course.

558
00:49:32,840 --> 00:49:34,680
STYLE
::cue

559
00:49:39,480 --> 00:49:43,080
What are you doing here?
I told you to stay home.

560
00:49:43,160 --> 00:49:44,760
We're bored of staying home.

561
00:49:44,880 --> 00:49:46,640
And we like monkey berries.

562
00:49:46,720 --> 00:49:49,040
We aren't looking
for monkey berries.

563
00:49:49,120 --> 00:49:53,800
- But we might find some.
- All right, but stay close.

564
00:49:59,600 --> 00:50:01,160
Would you move it already?

565
00:50:01,240 --> 00:50:03,280
Those apes could have
thumped us by now.

566
00:50:06,480 --> 00:50:07,960
Whoa!

567
00:50:08,040 --> 00:50:09,520
Huh?

568
00:50:13,440 --> 00:50:14,800
Did we make it?

569
00:50:14,880 --> 00:50:17,800
Yep,
we'll be safe here.

570
00:50:18,800 --> 00:50:21,040
Boy, I sure missed you guys.

571
00:50:21,160 --> 00:50:23,160
We missed you too, pal.

572
00:50:23,240 --> 00:50:24,960
That's why we came
to bring you home.

573
00:50:25,080 --> 00:50:27,720
- Not coming home.
- You're not?

574
00:50:27,800 --> 00:50:31,160
Nope. I'm a Zugor now.

575
00:50:31,240 --> 00:50:33,320
A Zugor?
What does that mean?

576
00:50:33,400 --> 00:50:36,320
Means I don't need anybody
but myself.

577
00:50:36,400 --> 00:50:39,320
- Anybody?
- Anybody.

578
00:50:39,400 --> 00:50:41,200
Well, what about your mom?

579
00:50:48,520 --> 00:50:51,280
She's better off without me.

580
00:50:51,360 --> 00:50:55,360
And I can't go back.
I'm a Zugor now.

581
00:50:55,440 --> 00:50:58,600
Well, who is this
Zugor monster anyways?

582
00:50:58,680 --> 00:51:01,320
I told you,
he's not a monster.

583
00:51:01,400 --> 00:51:04,200
- There is no monster.
- No monster?

584
00:51:04,280 --> 00:51:06,520
What do you mean, no monster?

585
00:51:06,600 --> 00:51:08,080
Ah!

586
00:51:08,160 --> 00:51:11,720
Uh, well,
I mean there's no monster...

587
00:51:11,840 --> 00:51:14,880
- Bigger or scarier...
- Hey!

588
00:51:14,960 --> 00:51:17,440
Looky what I found.

589
00:51:17,520 --> 00:51:20,720
Put me down.
Put me down!

590
00:51:20,800 --> 00:51:22,280
Okay.

591
00:51:26,840 --> 00:51:30,600
Ah! What the...?
Why? Who?

592
00:51:30,680 --> 00:51:31,880
- Hello.
- Ah!

593
00:51:37,360 --> 00:51:39,880
- Zugor...
- You said you wouldn't
tell anybody.

594
00:51:39,960 --> 00:51:41,920
- You promised.
- Zugor, I'm sorry.

595
00:51:42,000 --> 00:51:45,840
- I didn't mean to...
- You're the Zugor?

596
00:51:45,920 --> 00:51:47,920
All this time
my poor boys and I

597
00:51:48,040 --> 00:51:52,320
have been stuck in that
rotten valley because of you?

598
00:51:52,400 --> 00:51:54,280
I ought to...

599
00:51:56,720 --> 00:51:59,920
- Leave him alone!
- Out of the way, twerp.

600
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:02,360
Mmm, you know what, boys?

601
00:52:02,440 --> 00:52:08,080
I think this place could use
a little... remodeling.

602
00:52:08,160 --> 00:52:09,760
Oh, yeah!

603
00:52:09,840 --> 00:52:12,240
Oh, good. Oh, good.

604
00:52:16,440 --> 00:52:20,680
Hey, Kago, look at this.

605
00:52:20,760 --> 00:52:24,200
It's bouncy, bouncy,
bounce...

606
00:52:34,920 --> 00:52:40,720
You see, it's not nice
to fool Mama Gunda.

607
00:52:40,800 --> 00:52:43,160
- Zugor?
- This is your fault.

608
00:52:43,240 --> 00:52:44,560
I'm sorry.

609
00:52:44,680 --> 00:52:46,920
I needed to help my friends
and I...

610
00:52:54,320 --> 00:52:57,840
Oh, so that's
where all of you are from.

611
00:52:57,920 --> 00:53:00,280
Oh, how lovely.

612
00:53:00,360 --> 00:53:01,920
Thanks to blabbermouth here

613
00:53:02,000 --> 00:53:05,000
we know where to find
our new home.

614
00:53:05,120 --> 00:53:07,040
They squeezed it out of me.

615
00:53:07,160 --> 00:53:11,240
Come on, boys.
Let's go take over
the neighborhood.

616
00:53:11,320 --> 00:53:16,560
And this time
no one gets in our way.

617
00:53:22,120 --> 00:53:25,280
There it is.
Dark Mountain.

618
00:53:30,480 --> 00:53:33,960
Zugor!
Zugor, where are you?
STYLE
::cue

619
00:53:35,160 --> 00:53:37,280
Zugor.

620
00:53:37,400 --> 00:53:39,440
First rule...

621
00:53:41,320 --> 00:53:44,720
Zugor, come on.
We need your help.

622
00:53:44,800 --> 00:53:47,240
Tarzan,
we're gonna go warn Kerchak.

623
00:53:47,320 --> 00:53:48,520
Wait. We're coming with you.

624
00:53:48,600 --> 00:53:51,720
Uh, no offense, Tarzan,
but you'll just slow us down.

625
00:53:51,800 --> 00:53:54,040
- Let's go, Tant.
- Whoa.

626
00:53:54,120 --> 00:53:56,440
They won't make it in time.

627
00:53:56,520 --> 00:53:58,520
You're the only one
who knows this mountain.

628
00:53:58,600 --> 00:54:01,760
No. I never should have
let you in.

629
00:54:01,840 --> 00:54:04,920
I thought you were my friend
and you betrayed me.

630
00:54:06,760 --> 00:54:11,240
It was the First Rule,
and I broke it.

631
00:54:11,320 --> 00:54:13,120
Zugor, please.

632
00:54:13,200 --> 00:54:16,760
I know I messed everything up,
but you've got to help.

633
00:54:16,840 --> 00:54:18,000
Boo-hoo.

634
00:54:18,080 --> 00:54:19,680
It's my family.

635
00:54:19,760 --> 00:54:21,520
Then go. Go!

636
00:54:21,600 --> 00:54:24,560
You don't need me!
And I don't need you!

637
00:54:26,440 --> 00:54:28,680
Fine.

638
00:55:14,400 --> 00:55:17,920
Boo-hoo for me.

639
00:55:26,240 --> 00:55:28,440
I think I know which way to go.

640
00:55:28,520 --> 00:55:29,440
Yeah, me too.

641
00:55:29,520 --> 00:55:30,680
It's that way.

642
00:55:30,760 --> 00:55:32,160
Come on, guys.
I know a shortcut.

643
00:55:32,240 --> 00:55:34,920
- Tarzan!
- Oh, no! Ah!

644
00:55:35,000 --> 00:55:38,480
Whoa!

645
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:44,120
Whoa!

646
00:55:55,640 --> 00:55:57,680
Let's never speak of this again.

647
00:55:58,320 --> 00:56:00,480
Come on.

648
00:56:01,960 --> 00:56:02,720
Oof!

649
00:56:05,680 --> 00:56:08,200
Slow, down.
Don't get too far ahead.

650
00:56:08,280 --> 00:56:10,720
- I won't.
- Huh?

651
00:56:10,800 --> 00:56:12,880
Hey, look Ma, a baby.

652
00:56:12,960 --> 00:56:14,760
Well, for goodness sakes.

653
00:56:14,840 --> 00:56:16,600
Oh, can I play with it?

654
00:56:16,680 --> 00:56:18,880
- Can I?
- Put him down.

655
00:56:18,960 --> 00:56:20,920
Says who?

656
00:56:23,720 --> 00:56:25,920
Hey.

657
00:56:26,000 --> 00:56:27,560
- Back off.
- Yeah!

658
00:56:27,640 --> 00:56:30,080
You can't do that to my brother.

659
00:56:31,480 --> 00:56:34,800
- Ah!
- Mom!

660
00:56:38,160 --> 00:56:41,240
- Mom, are you okay?
- Tarzan!

661
00:56:41,320 --> 00:56:42,880
Oh, goody.

662
00:56:43,000 --> 00:56:46,720
- Leave him alone!
- Let's see if he can fly.

663
00:56:46,800 --> 00:56:48,600
Mom!

664
00:56:49,920 --> 00:56:53,440
- Zugor!
- Hmm?

665
00:56:53,520 --> 00:56:54,760
Ha-ha!

666
00:57:03,520 --> 00:57:05,640
- Zugor?
- Tarzan!

667
00:57:05,720 --> 00:57:07,400
But, what are you...?

668
00:57:07,480 --> 00:57:08,800
Ha-ha! I did it!

669
00:57:08,880 --> 00:57:11,640
I finally figured out
what you are!

670
00:57:11,720 --> 00:57:15,560
A Tarzan!

671
00:57:15,640 --> 00:57:17,440
- A Tarzan?
- Yes.

672
00:57:17,520 --> 00:57:19,400
Remember how you saved us
from that rhino?

673
00:57:19,480 --> 00:57:21,440
And made
that great hammock?

674
00:57:21,520 --> 00:57:23,160
And got those bananas?

675
00:57:23,240 --> 00:57:25,120
You do things no one else can.

676
00:57:25,200 --> 00:57:28,240
Kid, you're a Tarzan.
STYLE
::cue

677
00:57:28,320 --> 00:57:31,040
Now, go get 'em.

678
00:57:42,520 --> 00:57:44,520
Hmm?

679
00:57:44,600 --> 00:57:46,000
- Hey!
- Huh?

680
00:57:46,080 --> 00:57:48,320
Hey!

681
00:57:48,400 --> 00:57:49,760
It's him.

682
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:57,520
Ah!

683
00:57:59,760 --> 00:58:02,960
Get out of here,
you ratty old thing.

684
00:58:03,080 --> 00:58:04,320
Ratty?

685
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:07,560
You hit every branch when you
fell out of the ugly tree.

686
00:58:07,640 --> 00:58:08,920
Well, you're so bony

687
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:11,000
I bet the vultures
wouldn't even want you.

688
00:58:11,080 --> 00:58:13,280
Ha! Hey, the hippo called.

689
00:58:13,360 --> 00:58:15,920
He wants his body back.

690
00:58:18,000 --> 00:58:21,200
Hold on, little ones.

691
00:58:21,280 --> 00:58:24,520
Auntie Kala.
Auntie Kala!

692
00:58:31,720 --> 00:58:33,200
Ow, ow, ow, ow.

693
00:58:33,280 --> 00:58:36,000
Come on. Climb up.

694
00:58:39,640 --> 00:58:41,240
Huh?

695
00:58:44,160 --> 00:58:46,000
Ah!

696
00:58:49,440 --> 00:58:51,520
Ah!

697
00:58:53,120 --> 00:58:55,800
Put a cork in it,
you scraggly old sloth.

698
00:58:55,880 --> 00:58:58,960
You big blob of swamp gas.

699
00:58:59,040 --> 00:59:01,160
Lizard lips!

700
00:59:01,240 --> 00:59:03,320
- Slug snot!
- Bat barf!

701
00:59:03,400 --> 00:59:05,640
You have beautiful eyes!

702
00:59:05,720 --> 00:59:06,880
- Hmm?
- Huh?

703
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:08,640
- Eh?
- Mmm?

704
00:59:08,720 --> 00:59:12,480
Oh, this is creepy.
What is he?

705
00:59:12,560 --> 00:59:14,680
Where is he?

706
00:59:14,760 --> 00:59:16,640
What was that?

707
00:59:18,320 --> 00:59:21,320
Ah! Mama!

708
00:59:30,640 --> 00:59:32,040
Hey!

709
00:59:34,920 --> 00:59:37,080
Uh-oh.

710
00:59:37,160 --> 00:59:39,880
Ow! Ow! Oh!

711
00:59:39,960 --> 00:59:42,840
Oh! Oh! Oh! Ow! Ooh!

712
00:59:53,280 --> 00:59:55,040
Ow!

713
01:00:00,320 --> 01:00:01,200
Huh?

714
01:00:03,040 --> 01:00:03,880
Ah!

715
01:00:03,960 --> 01:00:06,680
Uto, wait for me!

716
01:00:07,680 --> 01:00:08,840
Ah!

717
01:00:12,960 --> 01:00:15,000
Auntie Kala, hang on!

718
01:00:37,000 --> 01:00:39,080
- Mom!
- Kala!

719
01:00:39,200 --> 01:00:42,200
Ah!

720
01:00:44,760 --> 01:00:48,320
Yes!
Way to go, Tarzan!

721
01:00:57,400 --> 01:00:59,000
Oh, I thought I'd lost you.

722
01:00:59,080 --> 01:01:01,200
I'm sorry I left, Mom.

723
01:01:01,280 --> 01:01:03,200
But I didn't want to hurt you.

724
01:01:03,280 --> 01:01:05,040
Hurt me?

725
01:01:05,120 --> 01:01:08,200
Tarzan, you saved me.

726
01:01:09,440 --> 01:01:11,880
- Mama!
STYLE
::cue
- Mama!

727
01:01:11,960 --> 01:01:16,840
- Mama! Help!
- He's after us.

728
01:01:16,920 --> 01:01:19,760
Ah! He's everywhere!

729
01:01:19,840 --> 01:01:21,640
Hello, boys.

730
01:01:21,720 --> 01:01:23,920
Mama?

731
01:01:24,000 --> 01:01:27,560
He thinks I have beautiful eyes.

732
01:01:35,040 --> 01:01:38,120
Ah...

733
01:01:38,200 --> 01:01:40,640
Wait a second.
Aren't we gonna thump somebody?

734
01:01:40,720 --> 01:01:43,080
- Yeah.
- Oh no, dears.

735
01:01:43,160 --> 01:01:46,040
- That's all over now.
- But Ma!

736
01:01:46,120 --> 01:01:48,800
Lips!

737
01:01:48,880 --> 01:01:52,160
How many times do I have
to tell you no fighting?

738
01:01:52,240 --> 01:01:55,840
No more fighting with anyone.

739
01:01:55,920 --> 01:01:58,480
Yes, ma'am.

740
01:02:03,440 --> 01:02:07,440
The timeless mystery of love.

741
01:02:07,520 --> 01:02:08,840
Ew.

742
01:02:08,920 --> 01:02:11,520
Mmm...

743
01:02:25,360 --> 01:02:27,800
Okay, wait,
I think I've got it.

744
01:02:27,880 --> 01:02:31,040
You thought you were a nothing,
but you're really a something,

745
01:02:31,120 --> 01:02:33,280
which makes you an anything?

746
01:02:33,360 --> 01:02:36,120
- No, no, Mom.
- What was it again?

747
01:02:36,200 --> 01:02:37,800
Oh, it doesn't matter.

748
01:02:37,880 --> 01:02:39,400
You were right after.

749
01:02:39,480 --> 01:02:43,800
What I am,
is part of this family.

750
01:02:43,880 --> 01:02:47,640
Oh, Tarzan,
I am so proud of you.

751
01:02:50,080 --> 01:02:53,440
- Zugor!
- Tarzan.

752
01:02:53,520 --> 01:02:56,080
- I came to say goodbye.
- Already?

753
01:02:56,160 --> 01:02:58,560
Well, you know.

754
01:03:01,240 --> 01:03:03,200
They need me.

755
01:03:05,400 --> 01:03:08,320
- I'll be up to visit you soon.
- You better.

756
01:03:08,400 --> 01:03:10,760
Oh, and, Zugor...

757
01:03:10,840 --> 01:03:13,680
Thanks.
Thanks for everything.

758
01:03:13,760 --> 01:03:16,880
No. Thank you.

759
01:03:23,000 --> 01:03:25,920
Now boys, the two of you
are going to fix

760
01:03:26,000 --> 01:03:27,840
that nice tree of Zugor's

761
01:03:27,920 --> 01:03:30,280
that you broke all to pieces.

762
01:03:30,360 --> 01:03:32,160
- But Ma...
- Boys.

763
01:03:32,240 --> 01:03:35,680
Never talk back to your mother.

764
01:03:35,760 --> 01:03:37,200
- Wait, we didn't...
- Boo-hoo.

765
01:03:37,280 --> 01:03:38,800
- We just...
- Boo-hoo.

766
01:03:38,880 --> 01:03:40,800
Boo-hoo for you.

767
01:03:40,920 --> 01:03:44,520
Rah!
Nothing escapes the monster!

768
01:03:46,440 --> 01:03:48,480
Really?

769
01:03:55,760 --> 01:03:57,840
What in the world
was that?

770
01:03:57,920 --> 01:04:01,240
That, my friend,
is a Tarzan.

771
01:05:19,960 --> 01:05:23,640
I'll sink or swim  But I'll keep looking

772
01:06:08,920 --> 01:06:12,680
STYLE
::cue

